PS5 HDMI resolutions                                      [ps5-bazzite-deck]

1. 1440p120 (497.75 MHz) is allowed on FLAVA3; the bridge gets the same
   high-bandwidth setup as 4K60 (TMDS 1/40 clock ratio, scrambling).
2. FLAVA3: when the sink lists 1440p but not at 60 Hz, add the standard
   1440p60 timing (CVT reduced blanking, 241.5 MHz).
3. FLAVA3: the bridge places a 1440p picture as if the signal had CVT-RB
   back porches (80 px / 33 lines); move the sync pulses of other 1440p
   timings so they match (fixes the picture shifted right or down). Active
   area, totals and pixel clock are unchanged.
4. Skip modes the sink accepts only as YCbCr 4:2:0: the bridge always sends
   them labelled as RGB (half-width, discoloured picture). The next mode,
   usually 1080p, is used instead.
